{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cordial-vulpine-piglet","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/integration/rebar_reconciler cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:29-43` — Preserve required project value, override behavior, and cleanup. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/_fakes.py:1-19, 33-40, 68-75` — Preserve verbatim captured shapes, deep-copy isolation, matching signatures, and production injection seam. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_jira_fixtures.py:1-19, 86-92` — Preserve complementary secret scrub and top-level-parent presence/falsy oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_roundtrip.py:1-23` — Preserve production-path bidirectional comment/link/parent round trip. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_snapshot_contract.py:1-20, 133-140, 192-200` — Preserve producer-consumer shape contract and discriminating nested-comment/link/parent oracles. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_verified_fake_contract.py:1-23, 57-61` — Preserve shared-contract execution and deliberately divergent-fake negative control. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_leaves_invocable.py:1-7, 35-45` — Preserve distinction between linkage and observable invocability. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_link_sync.py:1-29, 122-131, 165-179` — Preserve desired outbound/inbound relation contracts and representative Jira shape. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_post_deletion_linkage.py:1-11, 30-36, 63-71` — Preserve exact surviving leaf registry and linkage-versus-invocability scope. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:1-19, 357-370, 493-496` — Preserve non-vacuous git-backed setup, lifecycle clock injection, and two-pass zero-write oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py:1-31, 84-90, 207-214, 246-261, 537-543, 561-566` — Preserve chained fixed-point purpose, ADF truncation protection, link direction, and no-churn/no-echo outcomes. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/_fakes.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_jira_fixtures.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_roundtrip.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_snapshot_contract.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_verified_fake_contract.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_leaves_invocable.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_link_sync.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_post_deletion_linkage.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"8ca0-b4d6-f7dc-4e68","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/integration/rebar_reconciler"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571065666773533,"uuid":"fae3d05b-6a77-4df1-9bc5-9f7e0604913b"}